# Web primitives

For new or changed primitives, read [design.md](../../design.md), the component source
and public exports, and [futrob-stylex](../skills/futrob-stylex/SKILL.md).

- Reuse existing `@futrob/ui` contracts before adding a primitive. Product compositions
  stay in their owning app module and use the repo creation skills.
- Use Base UI behavior for interactive primitives where appropriate. Inspect the
  installed component API before adopting shadcn output; restyle with existing StyleX
  tokens and typography rather than keeping generated visual defaults.
- Preserve keyboard behavior, focus management, accessible names and render callbacks
  when wrapping primitives. Keep variants closed and typed, with public class/style
  composition following the existing helpers.
- New primitives use `packages/ui/src/components/<name>/`. Keep existing files in their
  current locations unless the task calls for migration. Update public exports and
  relevant stories with [add-story](../skills/add-story/SKILL.md).
- UI primitives have no competition, permission or provider dependencies. Native
  primitives have a separate implementation under `apps/mobile/src/ui`.
